mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45E TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.363em; margin-left: 0.051em;\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-var\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2032\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-script></mjx-msup><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D460 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c5D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo data-mjx-alternate=\"1\">′</mo></msup><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo data-mjx-alternate=\"1\">′</mo></msup><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>, so the product does not depend on the\nfirst representative. (5) The second argument is handled in the same\nway.</li>\n</ol>\n</blockquote>","file":"ch3/rationals-as-classes.html"}